        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0150" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg44"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Rives to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose the translation
                    of a note received from the ministry of foreign affairs in reply to a note
                    addressed to the said ministry in December, 1905, by the former ambassador, Mr.
                    Bellamy Storer, requesting an explanation from the Imperial and Royal Government
                    of the reasons for the refusal of the custom authorities at Eger to permit a
                    cask of salted beef, produced and prepared in the United States, from entering
                    the imperial and royal dominions.</p>
                <p>As will be seen from the foreign office’s note, a decree dated July 5, 1906, has
                    been passed restricting the importation of cattle and of <pb facs="0151" n="45"
                        xml:id="pg45"/> fresh and prepared meat from non-European countries into
                    Austria; and that importations are only permitted by special permit from the
                    minister of the interior, and that an application must be made to the said
                    ministry in every case, and under conditions fixed by the ministry.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George Barclay
                    Rives.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d27-a1.xml" xpointer="d27-a1"/>
            </div>
